wrote \"cover both an absent and a populated digest context.\" That's two extra probes. It needs the **cross product** — `user` × `chats` = 4.\n\n```\n{{#if user}}      ...content...  {{/if}}\n{{#unless chats}} ...content...  {{/unless}}\n```\n\n| probe | result |\n|---|---|\n| user absent, chats absent | `unless chats` renders → **passes** |\n| user present, chats present | `if user` renders → **passes** |\n| **user absent, chats present** | **both empty → renders empty in production** |\n\nA diagonal probe passes at boot and ships a prompt that is empty for precisely the owners who have chats but no personalization. That is the same unsoundness `model-system-prompts` already reasons about at length for `unless user` — and I reintroduced it while extending that very requirement. Needs fixing in the delta and in task 2.5.\n\n## B. The snapshot table's growth model changes qualitatively, and I sold it as a win\n\nThe proposal says \"one snapshot row is minted per chat\" as though that's the good outcome. Relative to a per-turn digest it is. Relative to **today** it's a 100–1000× increase.\n\nToday the reuse key is `(owner, content_hash, source)` + availability, so one owner on one model with unchanged personalization shares **a single snapshot across every chat they have**. With a per-chat digest, every chat's prompt is distinct by construction, so every chat mints its own row storing the full prompt text (`system_prompt text NOT NULL`) — plus another per compaction.\n\n1000 chats × ~4–8KB ≈ 4–8MB per heavy user, in a table that is append-only with **no purge path** (research §4.2 flagged this). And the digest content is stored twice: once as the chats-row baseline, once rendered into each snapshot.\n\nNot a blocker — storage is cheap and the chats/messages tables dwarf it. But it belongs in Risks with the math, not in the proposal as a selling point.\n\n## D. Enabling is retroactive; disabling is not\n\nThe spec discloses one direction and not the other.\n\nTurn the